  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with PCA and avgpool, which reaches 0.591 accuracy and 0.573 F1, clearly above singleprofile PCA and transformer aggregation. The main remaining uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation can improve over PCA under this same favorable profile/aggregation setting. config_008 tests scGPT with multiprofile avgpool while holding model setting, profile setting, and aggregation fixed, so it directly exploits the current best direction and isolates the effect of RNA representation. This is a high-value use of the next experiment because it can either produce a new best RNA-only result or confirm PCA, guiding later multimodal and fusion choices with the remaining budget."
